028 #edb/ref 17592186213074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051059 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186213075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051059 #edb/ref 1031 "Rewriting Radical Expressions Using the Laws of Exponents" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051059 #edb/ref 1033 6206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051059 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7dc8672e-e7ec-5a52-965b-6b7d5fb00896" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110297 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1085" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110297 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\left(\\dfrac{2x}{3}\\right)^4$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110297 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dc436197-3170-5ed7-a8f8-2092dd72da21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110297 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{2x}{3})^{4} = ((2x)^{4})/(3^{4})\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((2x)^{4})/(3^{4}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{2^{4}x^{4}}{3^{4}} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{16x^{4}}{81}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110298 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1086" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110298 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\left(\\dfrac{y}{2}\\right)^3 \\left(\\dfrac{2y}{3}\\right)^2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110298 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d8ea34f-b406-5bc8-9c00-de65d72e9d6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110298 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{y}{2})^{3}(\\frac{2y}{3})^{2} = \\frac{y^{3}}{2^{3}} \\cdot ((2y)^{2})/(3^{2})\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{y^{3}}{2^{3}} \\cdot ((2y)^{2})/(3^{2}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{y^{3}}{8} \\cdot \\frac{2^{2}y^{2}}{9} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{3}}{8} \\cdot \\frac{4y^{2}}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{y^{3}}{8} \\cdot \\frac{4y^{2}}{9} &=  \\\\\n(4y^{(3 + 2)})/(72) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{4y^{5}}{72} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{5}}{18}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1039 "Using the Power of Quotient Rule with One Fraction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110659 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "95f11186-e295-5091-93c3-07072b0c18eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1039 "Using the Power of Quotient Rule with Two Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110660 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "422bde20-bd83-5a20-b708-734b585ac256" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1045 "The Power of Quotient Rule With Algebraic Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110819 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f40ffb7e-1747-5f74-b124-0acd55b121f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111591 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111591 #edb/ref 1061 3552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b35013c-5ff4-5a7c-99fa-9b6c887c8c75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111592 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111592 #edb/ref 1061 3553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111592 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8fb38c77-55f0-5928-8c35-70c3ff0de790" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111592 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111593 #edb/ref 1061 3556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d9b9bca6-86d4-5640-8cb5-7659bf64aa00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111823 #edb/ref 1064 "The **power of quotient rule** states that if we want to raise the quotient\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{y}\n$$\n\nto some power $n$, we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power $n$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}\n$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}\n$$\n\nTo see why the power of quotient rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\frac{x}{y})^{4} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{x}{y} \\cdot \\frac{x}{y} \\cdot \\frac{x}{y} \\cdot \\frac{x}{y} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{x \\cdot x \\cdot x \\cdot x}{y \\cdot y \\cdot y \\cdot y} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{4}}{y^{4}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111823 #edb/ref 1065 1484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111823 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9aedc7af-544c-5314-a986-2cd6ce64479b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111823 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
